ok these are the most  in your face references from Naughty Dog  in uncharted 4 but you'll actually find  far more references to their games if  you look a little deeper in fact all  three of these franchises have way more  to offer in this game let's find them  The Last of Us is the wand which is  featured the most prominently over in  Chapter 12 gopher died near the sunken  ship and you'll find a skeleton with  some peculiar fungus growing out of its  face  this is a pretty clear reference to the  last of us and the infamous clickers the  infected creatures that scared the crap  out of us and probably killed you many  times or just me I died a lot in that  game how about something a little less  gross well this is quite spoilery  because it's in the epilogue of the game  so this is your chance now to run away  before I end this sentence have they  gone  they've gone okay in the game's epilogue  when you take control of Nate's daughter  Cassie you'll get the chance to explore  her room take a closer look at some of  those posters she has pinned up and  you'll see one for The Last of Us  American daughter's a comic book made by  Dark Horse sadly seems this asset was  made just for uncharted 4 and American  daughters doesn't exist well not yet  because I'm writing this before the Last  of Us part two comes out but Dark Horse  did publish a series of comics called  The Last of Us American Dreams which  serves as a prequel to the main game so  this makes them a little more real than  the other comic book think posters that  Cassie has around here such as savage  starlight - which you may recognize as  one of the comics Ellie read in The Last  of Us only for it to leave her in an  agonizing cliffhanger to be continued  well it looks like he got a sequel  I wonder if Ellie will get around to  reading it in the last of his part to  the other last of his references are  actually way more subtle than this and  super easy to miss later on in the game  when Nate and Elena are adventuring as a  duo  Elena briefly brings up one of her  previous jobs  Elena reveals she worked at a restaurant  called macho nacho this sounds like the  first job you have the producer on your  TV show no my manager from macho nacho  you worked at a macho nacho then in a  later flashback scene a young Nate can  find a medicine bottle that's from  Western pharmacy believe it or not both  of these companies actually exist in the  world of The Last of Us Ellie can easily  find stars for both of them in the games  Left Behind DLC so do The Last of Us and  Uncharted take place in the same  universe it's a stretch I know but I'm  on board with this I think they are the  same timeline  uncharted 4 other jak &amp; daxter reference  is another blinkin you're missing moment  in the first chapter you'll find a  cupboard full of board games some of the  references here are more obvious than  others there's one call  democracy which you would usually call  monopoly but tucked away just below it  you can see the jak and Daxter boardgame  weirdly enough a jak and daxter board  game also appears in the Last of Us  which again suggests this is all one big  same timeline universe thing but then  there's also an uncharted board game in  The Last of Us  so maybe I'm thinking too far into this  okay I'll stop let's move on as for the  remaining Crash Bandicoot reference well  that one's a little bit more  in-your-face and I know if I didn't put  this in the video people would be up in  arms it's not really an easter egg it's  a slap in the face shout out to Crash  Bandicoot during chapter four after Nate  has spent a few minutes wandering around  his attic and admiring his handiwork  from the previous Uncharted games he  heads downstairs to find Elena firing up  a ps1 or as Nate puts it a TV game thing  I don't need to know what it's called  I've seen you play it's jumping and  running and I have a natural talent for  that this is just nostalgia it's  beautiful the attention to detail is  ridiculous just listen to this sound oh  it still gives me goosebumps to this day  it's not just an awesome tribute to a  classic video game it's also testimony  to just how far video games have come  even if some of them still involve  running straight towards the camera and  avoiding obstacles well now we've got  Naughty Dog's all the titles out of the  way you'd think that would be the end of  this self referential cycle were in well  no not a chance  it seems fitting though given uncharted  4 slightly more nostalgic take on Nate's  adventures such as an entire scene  dedicated to looking back at his career  in the Attic some really good memories  there but on top of that even some of  Nate's jokes make reoccurring  appearances in uncharted 4 if you choose  to take a dip during chapter 12 Nate  will try and play the classic game Marco  Polo with Sam Marco this may seem like a  nothing moment well he's actually done  this in every game since uncharted 2  back then he tried it with Chloe and had  pretty much the same amount of success  back then hey check it out Marco  really  in uncharted 3 he did this again all by  himself anyway let's move on from  Naughty Dog's ego and take a look at  other Easter eggs and references in  chapter 11  wander over to the passport bureau and  you can hear Sully and Drake have this  little exchange could be worse it could  be our stowed sky arstotzka is actually  the fictional country that plays host to  the 2013 indie classics papers please  where you play as an immigration officer  reviewing immigrants as they try to  enter the country  looks like naughty dog have some love  for the little guy too and also while  we're here this location is home to one  of my favorite Easter Egg conversations  in the game grab an apple on the way to  the market and make sure Nate stops to  meet this friendly little lemur shortly  after that pesky little guy will come  running up to you and steal that Apple  from your grasp earning you the 